hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"21022","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Sirin, from Mabad ibn Sirin, from a man of the Ansar, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prescribed for sciatica that the tail of an Arab ram, neither small nor large, be taken, then melted, then divided into three parts, then each day on an empty stomach a part be drunk."
"21023","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Anas ibn Sirin informed us, from his brother Mabad ibn Sirin, from a man of the Ansar, from his father, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prescribed for sciatica that the tail of an Arab ram, neither large nor small, be taken, then melted, then divided into three parts, then each day on an empty stomach a part be drunk."
